{% extends 'user/Academics/program_detail.html.twig' %}

{% block title %}Bachelor of Science in Computer Engineering{% endblock %}
{% block default_hero_image %}images/Academics/bscpe.png{% endblock %}

{% block overview_default %}
<p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed text-lg mb-6">
                            The Bachelor of Science in Computer Engineering (BSCpE) is a program that embodies the science and technology of design, development, implementation, maintenance, and integration of software and hardware components in modern computing systems and computer-controlled equipment.
                        </p>

                        <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed text-lg mb-6">
                            This program will produce computer engineers who are versatile and knowledgeable in computer science and electrical engineering, as well as in the foundations of mathematics and sciences.
                        </p>

                        <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed text-lg">
                            Also, computer engineers are expected to be life-long learners to maintain their knowledge and skills within their chosen discipline.
                        </p>
{% endblock %}

{% block objectives_default %}
<p class="text-slate-600 text-lg mb-8">
                            Three to five years after graduation, the Computer Engineering alumni shall have:
                        </p>

                        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">

                            <div class="bg-slate-50 rounded-[2rem] p-6 border border-slate-100">
                                <h3 class="font-black text-feu-green mb-4 uppercase">
                                    Professional Growth
                                </h3>

                                <p class="text-slate-600">
                                    Engaged in the practice of Computer Engineering or technopreneurship and innovation.
                                </p>
                            </div>

                            <div class="bg-slate-50 rounded-[2rem] p-6 border border-slate-100">
                                <h3 class="font-black text-feu-green mb-4 uppercase">
                                    Leadership
                                </h3>

                                <p class="text-slate-600">
                                    Assumed significant roles with key responsibilities in their workplace.
                                </p>
                            </div>

                            <div class="bg-slate-50 rounded-[2rem] p-6 border border-slate-100">
                                <h3 class="font-black text-feu-green mb-4 uppercase">
                                    Organizations
                                </h3>

                                <p class="text-slate-600">
                                    Involved themselves in professional, socio-civic, government, or non-government organizations.
                                </p>
                            </div>

                            <div class="bg-slate-50 rounded-[2rem] p-6 border border-slate-100">
                                <h3 class="font-black text-feu-green mb-4 uppercase">
                                    Community Impact
                                </h3>

                                <p class="text-slate-600">
                                    Demonstrated continuous professional development through certifications, attendance to training, seminars, and conferences and/or pursuit of graduate studies in engineering or related fields.
                                </p>
                            </div>

                        </div>
{% endblock %}

{% block specializations_default %}
<div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">

                            <div class="bg-slate-50 rounded-[2rem] p-6 border border-slate-100">
                                <h3 class="font-black text-feu-green mb-4 uppercase">
                                    Internet of Things (IoT) & Data Analytics
                                </h3>

                                <p class="text-slate-600 mb-4">
                                    Internet of Things (IoT) is the concept of a giant network where interrelated computing devices, objects or people can transfer data over the network without the need for human-to-human or human-to-computer interaction.
                                </p>

                                <p class="text-slate-600 mb-4">
                                    Analytics, on another note, is the science of analyzing raw data, interpreting its meaningful patterns, aiming to provide meaningful insights to improve a business or a process.
                                </p>

                                <p class="text-slate-600">
                                    The BS Computer Engineering program, major in IoT and Analytics prepares students to be skilled professionals in the world where anything can be connected will be connected. This specialization will provide students a depth-track on Identifying problems that might be addressed by IoT Technology and Data Analysis to provide useful information and aid decision-making.
                                </p>
                            </div>

                            <div class="bg-slate-50 rounded-[2rem] p-6 border border-slate-100">
                                <h3 class="font-black text-feu-green mb-4 uppercase">
                                    Network Administration and Cybersecurity
                                </h3>

                                <p class="text-slate-600 mb-4">
                                    Network Administration is the discipline of administering and managing computer networks that includes provisioning of networks, performance management, troubleshooting, and sustaining the reliability of a network.
                                </p>

                                <p class="text-slate-600 mb-4">
                                    Cybersecurity goes hand in hand with Network Administration as it is the practice of protecting the digital platforms from theft or damage.
                                </p>

                                <p class="text-slate-600">
                                    The BS Computer Engineering program, major in Network Administration and Cybersecurity prepares students to perform a wide-array of tasks in the day-to-day operation of networks and cybersecurity. This program will shape them into highly effective future network administrators and cybersecurity experts who are critical thinkers, problem solvers, and innovators.
                                </p>
<div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">

                            <div class="bg-slate-50 rounded-[2rem] p-6 border border-slate-100">
                                <h3 class="font-black text-feu-green mb-4 uppercase">
